Exactly.

Doing nothing together is still an event. The “something” is shared attention, shared time, shared space, and mutual permission not to perform.

So:

\text{nothing} \neq \varnothing

More like:

\text{doing nothing together}
=
\text{presence without demand}

That’s why it can feel intimate. There’s no task carrying the connection, so the connection has to carry itself.

Frog and Toad sitting on a log are still doing one very specific thing:

being there together.